      "message": "When user is changed after new user is created, QSTileHost.onTuningChanged callback will be called and below sequence can be occured.\n - Run tile.destroy().  \n - Run  createTile(tileSpec).\n - But \"tile.destroy()\"\" use handler thread. So, CustomTile.create() can be called before old user`s customTile object`s handleDestroy().\n - So, TileServices.getTileWrapper(CustomTile tile) will be runed firstly. And new user`s tile(CustomTile object) will be added to TileServices`s mTiles list with the tile`s component name(key).\n - And then old user`s customTile`s handleDestroy() is called. So, TileServices.freeService(CustomTile tile, TileServiceManager service) will be called.\n - At that time, new user`s tile(CustomTile object) will be removed by \"mTiles.remove(tile.getComponent())\". Because component name is same between old user and new user.\n - After that, TileServices`s mTiles list don`t contain the customTile`s object. \n - So, when run requestListening(ComponentName component) ,  operation will be blocked by below code.\n            CustomTile customTile \u003d getTileForComponent(component);\n            if (customTile \u003d\u003d null) {\n                Log.d(\"TileServices\", \"Couldn\u0027t find tile for \" + component);\n                return;\n            }",
